# AimHigh AI Context Rules

## Stack Summary
- Frontend: multi-page static HTML + CSS + Vanilla JavaScript modules.
- Backend: Java 21 + Spring Boot, layered architecture Controller -> Service -> Repository.
- Data flow is API-first: UI never talks to database directly, only through REST endpoints.

## Architecture Boundaries
- Keep page UI logic in page-specific JS files under `AimHigh-IELTS-Website/js`.
- Keep transport logic in a centralized API client module (`api.js`).
- Keep business rules in Spring Service classes, not in Controller classes.
- Keep persistence logic in Repository/JPA layer only.

## Frontend <-> Backend Contract
- All frontend API calls must go through a shared request helper with base URL and timeout.
- Attach JWT from localStorage key `aimhigh_token` in `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.
- Use JSON request/response; set `Content-Type: application/json` for non-file payloads.
- Standard response envelope should be consistent: `{ success, message, data, errors, timestamp }`.
- Handle 401/403 globally and redirect to login page when session is invalid.

## API Change Workflow
- When adding an API: create DTOs -> implement Service -> expose Controller endpoint -> update JS API client -> update page module.
- Keep endpoint naming resource-based (`/api/exams`, `/api/attempts/{id}`), avoid action verbs in URI.
- Update SOURCE_CODE_MAP.md and relevant ai-docs rule files whenever contracts change.

## Quality and Safety Rules
- Validate input using Bean Validation annotations on request DTOs.
- Never return entities directly; return response DTOs only.
- Add unit/integration tests for new backend behavior and smoke test frontend flow.
- Do not break existing response fields without a migration note and frontend update.
